From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winspool, localspl: printer change notifications, and forms programs add

- FindFirstPrinterChangeNotification failed (INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, 525
  FIXMEs in the logs) and FindNext/FindClosePrinterChangeNotification and
  FreePrinterNotifyInfo were stubs. A notification is now an event the
  caller waits on, armed before the call returns: a thread watches the
  spool directory (a job's spool file appearing, written or going, from
  any process: ADD_JOB, WRITE_JOB/SET_JOB, DELETE_JOB) and the print
  registry keys (printers, forms, drivers, ports: ADD/SET/DELETE by whether
  entries came or went). FindNext says which changes, filtered by what was
  asked for; with notify options it gives a PRINTER_NOTIFY_INFO marked
  PRINTER_NOTIFY_INFO_DISCARDED (read everything again), which
  FreePrinterNotifyInfo frees.
- AddForm, SetForm and DeleteForm did nothing. Forms programs add are kept
  as values of the Print\Forms key (size, imageable area, order, flags),
  GetForm and EnumForms read them (FORM_USER, after the built-in ones, in
  the order added), adding an existing name fails with ERROR_FILE_EXISTS,
  a bad level or rectangle with ERROR_INVALID_LEVEL/PARAMETER, and the
  built-in forms are neither changed nor deleted. Without the right to
  write HKLM, the registry's error comes back.

Wine's winspool info tests: as before (three pre-existing failures).

Gate: test/printnotify-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_PRINTER_NOTIFY (winspool.drv/info.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_USER_FORMS (localspl/provider.c).
